-- title:
--   Homogeneous elements of an ideal generated by forms
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $\sigma$ an index type, and let $J_0$ be a set of polynomials in $A[x_\sigma] =$ `MvPolynomial σ A` each member of which is homogeneous of some degree: for every $G \in J_0$ there is an $e \in \mathbb{N}$ with `G.IsHomogeneous e`. Let $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $F$ be homogeneous of degree $d$ and lie in the ideal generated by $J_0$. Then there exist a finite set $s$ of polynomials, a function $e$ assigning a natural number to each polynomial, and a function $c$ assigning a polynomial to each polynomial, such that: $s$, viewed as a set, is contained in $J_0$; for every $G \in s$ one has $e\,G \le d$, $G$ is homogeneous of degree $e\,G$, and $c\,G$ is homogeneous of degree $d - e\,G$ (truncated subtraction, harmless since $e\,G \le d$); and $F = \sum_{G \in s} (c\,G) \cdot G$. Note that $e$ and $c$ are total functions on `MvPolynomial σ A`, their values being constrained only on $s$, and that the degrees $e\,G$ are returned as data rather than computed from $G$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a form lying in an ideal generated by forms is a combination of those generators with homogeneous coefficients of complementary degree, in the concrete setting of a polynomial ring over a commutative ring with its usual grading. It is used in the treatment of closed subschemes of projective space, where it lets one pass from membership in an ideal generated by forms to chart-wise identities in degree-zero localisations; it is cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.eq_ker_of_ideal_basicOpen_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.eq_ker_of_ideal_basicOpen_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.mem_span_sup_linearForm_iff_forall_app_eq_zero_of_maximal_growth`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSpace.mem_span_sup_linearForm_iff_forall_app_eq_zero_of_maximal_growth).
